      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MOVEHOME ESTATE AGENTS ... are honoured to offer a truly wonderful 5/6 bedroom extended semi-detached period family home spanning approx. 183 sq. mtrs to the local market. This property dates from the early 1900's and sits with pride on the renowned Grace Park Road and has the added benefit of a large east facing rear garden. Retaining many of its features throughout, this fantastic opportunity is simply ideal for the growing family because of its ideal space and location. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises of a welcoming hallway with ample storage facilities. Two large interconnecting reception rooms to the front are located off the main hall along with a separate dining room and downstairs bathroom. The rear kitchen area and extended dining room to the rear is a very pleasant surprise and enjoys access to the rear garden thats not overlooked. The downstairs is completed with an additional room and could be used for a bedroom/home office/study room. Upstairs, there is a spacious landing area which is flooded with natural light . There are five generous sized bedrooms and two additional bathrooms completing the accommodation on this level.\r\n\r\nThe gardens are a particular feature of the property with off street parking to the front and a well maintained east facing rear garden which is planted with mature trees and shrubs giving ample privacy. \r\n\r\nThe location is exceptional, with Grace Park Road offering a peaceful and mature residential setting while being within easy reach of Drumcondra Village and its excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, pubs, supermarkets, independent shops and everyday amenities. The property is also ideally positioned close to Clontarf, with the DART at Clontarf and the seafront all within easy reach, offering wonderful opportunities for coastal walks, recreation and leisure. The area is particularly well served by schools, sporting and recreational facilities, with Griffith Park, the Botanic Gardens, Tolka Park and Croke Park all readily accessible. There are excellent transport connections with numerous Dublin Bus routes, Drumcondra railway station and easy access to the M1 and M50, while Dublin Airport is also only a short drive away.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is essential to appreciate all this wonderful home has to offer and by appointment with MOVEHOME  ESTATE AGENTS  ... 01-8844690"
      },
